timeline.body:
I like that you factored the logic of Main() out into a helper, but lets take it a bit further so that the mutually exclusive code paths are more obvious, and so that the "execv happens so subsequent code may not run" is more obvious.
e.g. something like:
```
def Main(...):
  if ...:
    _RunForZip(...)
  elif ...:
    _RunForCoverage(...)
  else:
    _RunExecv(...)
```

Otherwise its harder to follow the logic -- bit of cases are sprinkled, before, during, and after the different possible execution paths through the layers. It's easy to skim over the Execute() call and see a bunch of subsequent logic and not realize that logic will never actually run due to execv() being called in an inner function.

